  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The lacy circle replaces solid double crochet increases with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " shells separated by chain loops, so by round 4 the disc is mostly open space. The six-point symmetry of the increase distribution makes the finished motif look like a snowflake from above. Because lace crochet collapses until "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blocked"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", pinning is not optional: it opens the chain loops to their full width and sets the snowflake silhouette."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK weight cotton, approximately 25 m per motif. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors, blocking mat, blocking pins."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4 rounds in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook = 14 cm diameter after blocking. Before blocking the motif may measure only 10-11 cm; this is normal. Blocking is part of the construction process for lace motifs, not an optional finishing step."
          }
        ]
      },
