          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Ch 3 (counts as first "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "tr"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " throughout). Work 11 tr into the ring. Pull tail to close. Join with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "slip-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "sl st"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to top of ch 3. (12 tr.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "*Ch 3, sl st into next tr*; repeat from * to * around. (12 ch-3 loops.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work into each ch-3 loop: (1 "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "double-crochet-uk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", 1 "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "half-treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "htr"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", 1 tr, 1 htr, 1 dc). Sl st to close each shell as you finish it if desired. (12 small shells of 5 sts each = 60 sts.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "*Ch 4, sl st into the tip tr of next shell*; repeat from * to * around. Fasten off. (12 ch-4 loops.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "slug": "crochet-motif-circle-lacy"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in the starting and finishing tails securely. Wet-block by soaking in cold water for 10 minutes, press out excess moisture in a clean towel, then pin each of the 12 chain loops open to a blocking mat. Use rust-proof pins. Leave overnight. The difference between an unblocked and a blocked lacy circle is dramatic; do not skip this step."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join lacy circles to each other by linking corresponding ch-4 loops with a short length of chain or a sl st join before the last round is complete. The open loops at round 4 provide natural attachment points without needing to sew through solid fabric."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hand wash in cool water with a small amount of mild detergent. Rinse gently without wringing. Block again after each wash if the shape needs resetting."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The lacy circle is a good preparation for the lace square motif, which uses the same chain-arch technique but at square corners. You can also combine lacy circles with solid flat circles in the same blanket, alternating the two types for a textured, mixed look."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
